@startuml

title Shop database - Generic status history and audit policy

!include ./_common.puml

enum StatusHistoryEntityType {
    purchase
    inventory_document
    production_order
}

entity StatusHistory {
    * id: int
    --
    * entityType: StatusHistoryEntityType
    * entityId: int
    oldStatus: string(100)?
    * newStatus: string(100)
    comment: text?
    * changedAt: DateTimeImmutable
    changedBy: User?
    * store: Store
}


Store ||--o{ StatusHistory : has status logs
User |o--o{ StatusHistory : changes status
StatusHistoryEntityType ||--o{ StatusHistory : classifies

note right of StatusHistory
  Universal status history table for business documents that only need
  generic status audit:
  Purchase, InventoryDocument, ProductionOrder.

  Uses entityType + entityId intentionally for MVP flexibility.
  Important limitation: database cannot enforce foreign key to different tables.
  Application code must validate that entityId exists for the selected entityType.

  Suggested rule:
  create a StatusHistory row every time document status changes.

  Order uses dedicated OrderHistory instead, because its timeline must
  capture all user/system/integration actions, not only status changes.
  Payment operations use PaymentHistory and are merged into Order/Purchase
  admin histories without overloading this status-only table.
end note

@enduml
